msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:437
msgid "Return ``True`` if the node has any attributes."
msgstr "Верните True, если узел имеет какие-либо атрибуты."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:442
msgid "Return ``True`` if the node has any child nodes."
msgstr "Верните True, если у узла есть дочерние узлы."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:447
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if *other* refers to the same node as this node. This is "
"especially useful for DOM implementations which use any sort of proxy "
"architecture (because more than one object can refer to the same node)."
msgstr ""
"Возвращайте ``True``, если *other* относится к тому же узлу, что и этот "
"узел. Это особенно полезно для реализаций DOM, которые используют любую "
"прокси-архитектуру (поскольку на один и тот же узел может ссылаться более "
"одного объекта)."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:453
msgid ""
"This is based on a proposed DOM Level 3 API which is still in the \"working "
"draft\" stage, but this particular interface appears uncontroversial.  "
"Changes from the W3C will not necessarily affect this method in the Python "
"DOM interface (though any new W3C API for this would also be supported)."
msgstr ""
"Он основан на предложенном API DOM уровня 3, который все еще находится на "
"стадии «рабочего проекта», но этот конкретный интерфейс кажется бесспорным. "
"Изменения W3C не обязательно повлияют на этот метод в интерфейсе DOM Python "
"(хотя любой новый API W3C для этого также будет поддерживаться)."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:461
msgid ""
"Add a new child node to this node at the end of the list of children, "
"returning *newChild*. If the node was already in the tree, it is removed "
"first."
msgstr ""
"Добавьте новый дочерний узел к этому узлу в конце списка дочерних элементов, "
"вернув *newChild*. Если узел уже был в дереве, он сначала удаляется."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:468
msgid ""
"Insert a new child node before an existing child.  It must be the case that "
"*refChild* is a child of this node; if not, :exc:`NotFoundErr` is raised. "
"*newChild* is returned. If *refChild* is ``None``, it inserts *newChild* at "
"the end of the children's list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:476
msgid ""
"Remove a child node.  *oldChild* must be a child of this node; if not, :exc:"
"`NotFoundErr` is raised.  *oldChild* is returned on success.  If *oldChild* "
"will not be used further, its :meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.unlink` method "
"should be called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:484
msgid ""
"Replace an existing node with a new node. It must be the case that  "
"*oldChild* is a child of this node; if not, :exc:`NotFoundErr` is raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:490
msgid ""
"Join adjacent text nodes so that all stretches of text are stored as single :"
"class:`Text` instances.  This simplifies processing text from a DOM tree for "
"many applications."
msgstr ""
"Соединяйте соседние текстовые узлы, чтобы все фрагменты текста сохранялись "
"как отдельные экземпляры :class:`Text`. Это упрощает обработку текста из "
"дерева DOM для многих приложений."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:497
msgid ""
"Clone this node.  Setting *deep* means to clone all child nodes as well.  "
"This returns the clone."
msgstr ""
"Клонируйте этот узел. Установка *deep* означает также клонирование всех "
"дочерних узлов. Это возвращает клон."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:504
msgid "NodeList Objects"
msgstr "Объекты NodeList"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:509
msgid ""
"A :class:`NodeList` represents a sequence of nodes.  These objects are used "
"in two ways in the DOM Core recommendation:  an :class:`Element` object "
"provides one as its list of child nodes, and the :meth:`~Element."
"getElementsByTagName` and :meth:`~Element.getElementsByTagNameNS` methods "
"of :class:`Node` return objects with this interface to represent query "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:515
msgid ":class:`NodeList` does *not* inherit from :class:`Node`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:517
msgid ""
"The DOM Level 2 recommendation defines one method and one attribute for "
"these objects:"
msgstr ""
"Рекомендация DOM уровня 2 определяет один метод и один атрибут для этих "
"объектов:"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:523
msgid ""
"Return the *i*'th item from the sequence, or ``None`` if *i* is out of "
"range. Negative indices are not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:530
msgid "The number of nodes in the sequence."
msgstr "Количество узлов в последовательности."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:532
msgid ""
"In addition, the Python DOM interface requires that some additional support "
"is provided to allow :class:`NodeList` objects to be used as Python "
"sequences.  All :class:`NodeList` implementations must include support for :"
"meth:`~object.__len__` and :meth:`~object.__getitem__`; this allows "
"iteration over the :class:`NodeList` in :keyword:`for` statements and proper "
"support for the :func:`len` built-in function."
msgstr ""
"Кроме того, интерфейс DOM Python требует предоставления некоторой "
"дополнительной поддержки, позволяющей использовать объекты :class:`NodeList` "
"в качестве последовательностей Python. Все реализации :class:`NodeList` "
"должны включать поддержку :meth:`~object.__len__` и :meth:`~object."
"__getitem__`; это позволяет перебирать :class:`NodeList` в операторах :"
"keyword:`for` и обеспечивает правильную поддержку встроенной функции :func:"
"`len`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:540
msgid ""
"If a DOM implementation supports modification of the document, the :class:"
"`NodeList` implementation must also support the :meth:`~object.__setitem__` "
"and :meth:`~object.__delitem__` methods."
msgstr ""
"Если реализация DOM поддерживает модификацию документа, реализация :class:"
"`NodeList` должна также поддерживать методы :meth:`~object.__setitem__` и :"
"meth:`~object.__delitem__`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:548
msgid "DocumentType Objects"
msgstr "Объекты DocumentType"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:553
msgid ""
"Information about the notations and entities declared by a document "
"(including the external subset if the parser uses it and can provide the "
"information) is available from a :class:`DocumentType` object.  The :class:"
"`DocumentType` for a document is available from the :class:`Document` "
"object's :attr:`~Document.doctype` attribute; if there is no ``DOCTYPE`` "
"declaration for the document, the document's :attr:`~Document.doctype` "
"attribute will be set to ``None`` instead of an instance of this interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:561
msgid ""
":class:`DocumentType` is a specialization of :class:`Node`, and adds the "
"following attributes:"
msgstr ""
":class:`DocumentType` является специализацией :class:`Node` и добавляет "
"следующие атрибуты:"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:567
msgid ""
"The public identifier for the external subset of the document type "
"definition, or ``None`` if the ``DOCTYPE`` declaration does not specify it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:573
msgid ""
"The system identifier, a URI, for the external subset of the document type "
"definition, or ``None`` if the ``DOCTYPE`` declaration does not specify it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:579
msgid ""
"A string giving the complete internal subset from the document. This does "
"not include the brackets which enclose the subset.  If the document has no "
"internal subset, this should be ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Строка, дающая полное внутреннее подмножество документа. Сюда не входят "
"скобки, заключающие подмножество. Если документ не имеет внутреннего "
"подмножества, это значение должно быть «Нет»."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:586
msgid ""
"The name of the root element as given in the ``DOCTYPE`` declaration, if "
"present."
msgstr ""
"Имя корневого элемента, указанное в объявлении DOCTYPE, если оно "
"присутствует."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:592
msgid ""
"This is a :class:`NamedNodeMap` of :class:`Entity` nodes giving the "
"definitions of external entities. For entity names defined more than once, "
"only the first definition is provided (others are ignored as required by the "
"XML recommendation).  This may be ``None`` if the information is not "
"provided by the parser, or if no entities are defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:602
msgid ""
"This is a :class:`NamedNodeMap` of :class:`Notation` nodes giving the "
"definitions of notations. For notation names defined more than once, only "
"the first definition is provided (others are ignored as required by the XML "
"recommendation).  This may be ``None`` if the information is not provided by "
"the parser, or if no notations are defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:613
msgid "Document Objects"
msgstr "Объекты документа"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:618
msgid ""
"A :class:`Document` represents an entire XML document, including its "
"constituent elements, attributes, processing instructions, comments etc.  "
"Remember that it inherits properties from :class:`Node`."
msgstr ""
":class:`Document` представляет собой весь XML-документ, включая составляющие "
"его элементы, атрибуты, инструкции обработки, комментарии и т. д. Помните, "
"что он наследует свойства от :class:`Node`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:625
msgid "The one and only root element of the document."
msgstr "Единственный корневой элемент документа."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:630
msgid ""
"The :class:`DocumentType` node of the document, or ``None``. This is a read-"
"only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:636
msgid ""
"The :class:`DOMImplementation` object which created this document. This is a "
"read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:642
msgid "Whether error checking is enforced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:647
msgid "The location of the document, or ``None`` if it is unknown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:652
msgid "Create and return an empty :class:`DocumentFragment` node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:657
msgid "Create and return a :class:`CDATASection` node containing *data*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:662
msgid ""
"Return a copy of *importedNode* which belongs to this document. The original "
"node is not removed from its document. If *deep* is true, the descendants of "
"the node are copied too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:669
msgid ""
"Create and return a new element node.  The element is not inserted into the "
"document when it is created.  You need to explicitly insert it with one of "
"the other methods such as :meth:`~Node.insertBefore` or :meth:`~Node."
"appendChild`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:676
msgid ""
"Create and return a new element with a namespace.  The *tagName* may have a "
"prefix.  The element is not inserted into the document when it is created.  "
"You need to explicitly insert it with one of the other methods such as :meth:"
"`~Node.insertBefore` or :meth:`~Node.appendChild`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:684
msgid ""
"Create and return a text node containing the data passed as a parameter.  As "
"with the other creation methods, this one does not insert the node into the "
"tree."
msgstr ""
"Создайте и верните текстовый узел, содержащий данные, переданные в качестве "
"параметра. Как и другие методы создания, этот узел не вставляется в дерево."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:691
msgid ""
"Create and return a comment node containing the data passed as a parameter.  "
"As with the other creation methods, this one does not insert the node into "
"the tree."
msgstr ""
"Создайте и верните узел комментария, содержащий данные, переданные в "
"качестве параметра. Как и другие методы создания, этот узел не вставляется в "
"дерево."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:698
msgid ""
"Create and return a processing instruction node containing the *target* and "
"*data* passed as parameters.  As with the other creation methods, this one "
"does not insert the node into the tree."
msgstr ""
"Создайте и верните узел инструкции обработки, содержащий *цель* и *данные*, "
"переданные в качестве параметров. Как и другие методы создания, этот узел не "
"вставляется в дерево."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:705
msgid ""
"Create and return an attribute node.  This method does not associate the "
"attribute node with any particular element.  You must use :meth:`~Element."
"setAttributeNode` on the appropriate :class:`Element` object to use the "
"newly created attribute instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:713
msgid ""
"Create and return an attribute node with a namespace.  The *tagName* may "
"have a prefix.  This method does not associate the attribute node with any "
"particular element.  You must use :meth:`~Element.setAttributeNode` on the "
"appropriate :class:`Element` object to use the newly created attribute "
"instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:721
msgid ""
"Return the element with the given ID, or ``None``. Only attributes declared "
"as being of type ID in the DTD or by :meth:`Element.setIdAttribute` are "
"searched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:728
msgid ""
"Search for all descendants (direct children, children's children, etc.) with "
"a particular element type name."
msgstr ""
"Поиск всех потомков (прямых дочерних элементов, дочерних элементов и т. д.) "
"с определенным именем типа элемента."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:734
msgid ""
"Search for all descendants (direct children, children's children, etc.) with "
"a particular namespace URI and localname.  The localname is the part of the "
"namespace after the prefix."
msgstr ""
"Найдите всех потомков (прямые дочерние элементы, дочерние элементы и т. д.) "
"с определенным URI пространства имен и локальным именем. Локальное имя — это "
"часть пространства имен после префикса."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:741
msgid ""
"Rename the element or attribute node *n* and return it. *namespaceURI* is "
"the new namespace URI, or :data:`~xml.dom.EMPTY_NAMESPACE` if the node does "
"not belong to a namespace. *name* is the new qualified name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:747
msgid ""
"Raise :exc:`WrongDocumentErr` if *n* was created by another document, and :"
"exc:`NotSupportedErr` if it is neither an element nor an attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:754
msgid "Element Objects"
msgstr "Объекты элементов"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:759
msgid ""
":class:`Element` is a subclass of :class:`Node`, so inherits all the "
"attributes of that class."
msgstr ""
":class:`Element` является подклассом :class:`Node`, поэтому наследует все "
"атрибуты этого класса."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:765
msgid ""
"The element type name.  In a namespace-using document it may have colons in "
"it. The value is a string."
msgstr ""
"Имя типа элемента. В документе, использующем пространство имен, в нем могут "
"быть двоеточия. Значение представляет собой строку."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:771
msgid ""
"Declare that the attribute *name* is of type ID, so that the element is "
"found by :meth:`Document.getElementById`. Raise :exc:`NotFoundErr` if the "
"element has no such attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:778
msgid ""
"The same as :meth:`~Element.setIdAttribute`, but for an attribute specified "
"by its namespace URI and local name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:784
msgid ""
"The same as :meth:`~Element.setIdAttribute`, but for an already retrieved "
"attribute node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:790 ../../library/xml.dom.rst:795
msgid "Same as equivalent method in the :class:`Document` class."
msgstr "То же, что эквивалентный метод в классе :class:`Document`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:800
msgid "Return ``True`` if the element has an attribute named by *name*."
msgstr "Верните ``True``, если элемент имеет атрибут с именем *name*."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:805
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the element has an attribute named by *namespaceURI* and "
"*localName*."
msgstr ""
"Возвращайте ``True``, если элемент имеет атрибут с именем *namespaceURI* и "
"*localName*."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:811
msgid ""
"Return the value of the attribute named by *name* as a string. If no such "
"attribute exists, an empty string is returned, as if the attribute had no "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Верните значение атрибута, названного *name*, в виде строки. Если такого "
"атрибута не существует, возвращается пустая строка, как если бы атрибут не "
"имел значения."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:817
msgid "Return the :class:`Attr` node for the attribute named by *attrname*."
msgstr "Верните узел :class:`Attr` для атрибута, названного *attrname*."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:822
msgid ""
"Return the value of the attribute named by *namespaceURI* and *localName* as "
"a string. If no such attribute exists, an empty string is returned, as if "
"the attribute had no value."
msgstr ""
"Верните значение атрибута, названного *namespaceURI* и *localName*, в виде "
"строки. Если такого атрибута не существует, возвращается пустая строка, как "
"если бы атрибут не имел значения."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:829
msgid ""
"Return an attribute value as a node, given a *namespaceURI* and *localName*."
msgstr ""
"Возвращает значение атрибута в виде узла, учитывая *namespaceURI* и "
"*localName*."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:834
msgid "Remove an attribute by name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:839
msgid ""
"Remove and return *oldAttr* from the attribute list, if present. If "
"*oldAttr* is not present, :exc:`NotFoundErr` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Удалите и верните *oldAttr* из списка атрибутов, если он присутствует. Если "
"*oldAttr* отсутствует, возникает :exc:`NotFoundErr`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:845
msgid ""
"Remove an attribute by name.  Note that it uses a localName, not a qname."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:850
msgid "Set an attribute value from a string."
msgstr "Установите значение атрибута из строки."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:855
msgid ""
"Add a new attribute node to the element, replacing an existing attribute if "
"necessary if the :attr:`~Attr.name` attribute matches.  If a replacement "
"occurs, the old attribute node will be returned.  If *newAttr* is already in "
"use, :exc:`InuseAttributeErr` will be raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:863
msgid ""
"Add a new attribute node to the element, replacing an existing attribute if "
"necessary if the :attr:`~Node.namespaceURI` and :attr:`~Attr.localName` "
"attributes match.  If a replacement occurs, the old attribute node will be "
"returned.  If *newAttr* is already in use, :exc:`InuseAttributeErr` will be "
"raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:872
msgid ""
"Set an attribute value from a string, given a *namespaceURI* and a *qname*. "
"Note that a qname is the whole attribute name.  This is different than above."
msgstr ""
"Установите значение атрибута из строки, заданной *namespaceURI* и *qname*. "
"Обратите внимание, что qname — это полное имя атрибута. Это отличается от "
"приведенного выше."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:879
msgid "Attr Objects"
msgstr "Объекты Attr"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:884
msgid ""
":class:`Attr` inherits from :class:`Node`, so inherits all its attributes."
msgstr ""
":class:`Attr` наследуется от :class:`Node`, то есть наследует все его "
"атрибуты."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:886
msgid ""
"Attribute nodes are not part of the document tree. They are contained in "
"the :attr:`~Node.attributes` map of an element, not in its children, and "
"their :attr:`~Node.parentNode`, :attr:`~Node.previousSibling` and :attr:"
"`~Node.nextSibling` are always ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:895
msgid ""
"The attribute name. In a namespace-using document it may include a colon."
msgstr ""
"Имя атрибута. В документе, использующем пространство имен, оно может "
"включать двоеточие."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:901
msgid ""
"The part of the name following the colon if there is one, else the entire "
"name. This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""
"Часть имени после двоеточия, если оно есть, иначе все имя. Это атрибут, "
"доступный только для чтения."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:908
msgid ""
"The part of the name preceding the colon if there is one, else the empty "
"string."
msgstr ""
"Часть имени, предшествующая двоеточию, если оно есть, иначе пустая строка."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:914
msgid ""
"Whether this attribute is of type ID, either because it is declared as such "
"in the DTD or because :meth:`Element.setIdAttribute` was used. This is a "
"read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:922
msgid ""
"The :class:`Element` node to which this attribute belongs, or ``None`` if it "
"is not used. This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:929
msgid ""
"Whether the value of the attribute was explicitly set in the document, as "
"opposed to being defaulted from the DTD. This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:936
msgid ""
"The text value of the attribute.  This is a synonym for the :attr:`~Node."
"nodeValue` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:943
msgid "NamedNodeMap Objects"
msgstr "Объекты NamedNodeMap"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:948
msgid ":class:`NamedNodeMap` does *not* inherit from :class:`Node`."
msgstr ":class:`NamedNodeMap` *не* наследуется от :class:`Node`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:953
msgid "The length of the attribute list."
msgstr "Длина списка атрибутов."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:958
msgid ""
"Return an attribute with a particular index.  The order you get the "
"attributes in is arbitrary but will be consistent for the life of a DOM.  "
"Each item is an attribute node.  Get its value with the :attr:`~Attr.value` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:965
msgid ""
"Return the node with the given :attr:`~Attr.name`, or ``None`` if there is "
"no such node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:971
msgid ""
"Return the node with the given namespace URI and local name, or ``None`` if "
"there is no such node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:977
msgid ""
"Add *node* to the map, using its :attr:`~Attr.name` as the key. Return the "
"node which it replaces, or ``None`` if it replaces no node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:983
msgid ""
"Add *node* to the map, using its namespace URI and local name as the key. "
"Return the node which it replaces, or ``None`` if it replaces no node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:990
msgid ""
"Remove and return the node with the given :attr:`~Attr.name`. Raise :exc:"
"`NotFoundErr` if there is no such node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:996
msgid ""
"Remove and return the node with the given namespace URI and local name. "
"Raise :exc:`NotFoundErr` if there is no such node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:999
msgid ""
"You can also use the standardized :meth:`!getAttribute\\*` family of methods "
"on the :class:`Element` objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1006
msgid "DocumentFragment Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1011
msgid ""
":class:`DocumentFragment` is a lightweight container of nodes. It is a "
"subclass of :class:`Node`. When it is inserted into the document tree, its "
"children are inserted instead of it, and it becomes empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1021
msgid "CharacterData Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1026
msgid ""
":class:`CharacterData` represents text-like data in the XML document. It is "
"a subclass of :class:`Node`, and the base class of :class:`Text`, :class:"
"`CDATASection` and :class:`Comment`. Such nodes cannot have child nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1034
msgid "The content of the node as a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1039
msgid ""
"The number of characters in :attr:`~CharacterData.data`. This is a read-only "
"attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1045
msgid ""
"Return the substring of :attr:`~CharacterData.data` of *count* characters "
"starting at *offset*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1051
msgid "Append the string *arg* to :attr:`~CharacterData.data`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1056
msgid "Insert the string *arg* into :attr:`~CharacterData.data` at *offset*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1061
msgid ""
"Remove *count* characters from :attr:`~CharacterData.data` starting at "
"*offset*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1067
msgid ""
"Replace *count* characters of :attr:`~CharacterData.data` starting at "
"*offset* with the string *arg*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1074
msgid "Comment Objects"
msgstr "Объекты комментариев"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1079
msgid ""
":class:`Comment` represents a comment in the XML document. It is a subclass "
"of :class:`CharacterData`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1085
msgid ""
"The content of the comment as a string.  The attribute contains all "
"characters between the leading ``<!-``\\ ``-`` and trailing ``-``\\ ``->``, "
"but does not include them."
msgstr ""
"Содержимое комментария в виде строки. Атрибут содержит все символы между "
"начальным ``<!-``\\ ``-`` и конечным ``-``\\ ``->``, но не включает их."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1093
msgid "Text and CDATASection Objects"
msgstr "Текстовые объекты и объекты CDATASection."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1101
msgid ""
"The :class:`Text` interface represents text in the XML document.  If the "
"parser and DOM implementation support the DOM's XML extension, portions of "
"the text enclosed in CDATA marked sections are stored in :class:"
"`CDATASection` objects. These two interfaces are identical, but provide "
"different values for the :attr:`~Node.nodeType` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1107
msgid ""
":class:`Text` extends the :class:`CharacterData` interface, and :class:"
"`CDATASection` extends :class:`Text`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1113
msgid "The content of the text node as a string."
msgstr "Содержимое текстового узла в виде строки."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1118
msgid ""
"The text of all :class:`Text` nodes logically adjacent to this node, "
"concatenated in document order. This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1125
msgid ""
"Replace the text of all :class:`Text` nodes logically adjacent to this node "
"with *content*, removing the other nodes. Return this node, or ``None`` if "
"*content* is empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1132
msgid ""
"Split this node into two nodes at *offset*, keeping the first part in this "
"node and returning a new sibling node with the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1138
msgid ""
"The use of a :class:`CDATASection` node does not indicate that the node "
"represents a complete CDATA marked section, only that the content of the "
"node was part of a CDATA section.  A single CDATA section may be represented "
"by more than one node in the document tree.  There is no way to determine "
"whether two adjacent :class:`CDATASection` nodes represent different CDATA "
"marked sections."
msgstr ""
"Использование узла :class:`CDATASection` не означает, что узел представляет "
"собой полный раздел, отмеченный CDATA, а означает лишь то, что содержимое "
"узла было частью раздела CDATA. Один раздел CDATA может быть представлен "
"более чем одним узлом в дереве документа. Невозможно определить, "
"представляют ли два соседних узла :class:`CDATASection` разные разделы, "
"отмеченные CDATA."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1148
msgid "ProcessingInstruction Objects"
msgstr "Объекты ProcessingInstruction "

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1153
msgid ""
"Represents a processing instruction in the XML document; this inherits from "
"the :class:`Node` interface and cannot have child nodes."
msgstr ""
"Представляет инструкцию обработки в документе XML; он наследуется от "
"интерфейса :class:`Node` и не может иметь дочерних узлов."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1159
msgid ""
"The content of the processing instruction up to the first whitespace "
"character. This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""
"Содержимое инструкции обработки до первого символа пробела. Это атрибут, "
"доступный только для чтения."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1165
msgid ""
"The content of the processing instruction following the first whitespace "
"character."
msgstr "Содержимое инструкции обработки после первого символа пробела."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1172
msgid "Entity Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1177
msgid ""
":class:`Entity` represents a parsed or unparsed entity declared in the DTD. "
"It is a subclass of :class:`Node`. Entity nodes are contained in :attr:"
"`DocumentType.entities` and cannot be inserted into the document tree. The "
"name of the entity is its :attr:`~Node.nodeName`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1186
msgid ""
"The public identifier of the entity, or ``None`` if it is not specified. "
"This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1193
msgid ""
"The system identifier of the entity, or ``None`` if it is not specified. "
"This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1200
msgid ""
"The name of the notation for an unparsed entity, or ``None`` for a parsed "
"entity. This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1208
msgid "Notation Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1213
msgid ""
":class:`Notation` represents a notation declared in the DTD. It is a "
"subclass of :class:`Node` and cannot have child nodes. Notation nodes are "
"contained in :attr:`DocumentType.notations` and cannot be inserted into the "
"document tree. The name of the notation is its :attr:`~Node.nodeName`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1222
msgid ""
"The public identifier of the notation, or ``None`` if it is not specified. "
"This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1229
msgid ""
"The system identifier of the notation, or ``None`` if it is not specified. "
"This is a read-only attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1237
msgid "Exceptions"
msgstr "Исключения"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1239
msgid ""
"The DOM Level 2 recommendation defines a single exception, :exc:"
"`DOMException`, and a number of constants that allow applications to "
"determine what sort of error occurred. :exc:`DOMException` instances carry "
"a :attr:`code` attribute that provides the appropriate value for the "
"specific exception."
msgstr ""
"Рекомендация DOM уровня 2 определяет одно исключение :exc:`DOMException` и "
"ряд констант, которые позволяют приложениям определять тип ошибки. "
"Экземпляры :exc:`DOMException` содержат атрибут :attr:`code`, который "
"предоставляет соответствующее значение для конкретного исключения."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1244
msgid ""
"The Python DOM interface provides the constants, but also expands the set of "
"exceptions so that a specific exception exists for each of the exception "
"codes defined by the DOM.  The implementations must raise the appropriate "
"specific exception, each of which carries the appropriate value for the :"
"attr:`code` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Интерфейс Python DOM предоставляет константы, но также расширяет набор "
"исключений, так что для каждого из кодов исключений, определенных DOM, "
"существует определенное исключение. Реализации должны вызывать "
"соответствующее исключение, каждое из которых несет соответствующее значение "
"атрибута :attr:`code`."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1253
msgid ""
"Base exception class used for all specific DOM exceptions.  This exception "
"class cannot be directly instantiated."
msgstr ""
"Базовый класс исключений, используемый для всех конкретных исключений DOM. "
"Этот класс исключений не может быть создан напрямую."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1259
msgid ""
"Raised when a specified range of text does not fit into a string. This is "
"not known to be used in the Python DOM implementations, but may be received "
"from DOM implementations not written in Python."
msgstr ""
"Возникает, когда указанный диапазон текста не помещается в строку. "
"Неизвестно, используется ли он в реализациях DOM Python, но может быть "
"получен из реализаций DOM, не написанных на Python."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1266
msgid ""
"Raised when an attempt is made to insert a node where the node type is not "
"allowed."
msgstr "Возникает при попытке вставить узел, тип узла которого не разрешен."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1272
msgid ""
"Raised when an index or size parameter to a method is negative or exceeds "
"the allowed values."
msgstr ""
"Возникает, когда параметр индекса или размера метода имеет отрицательное "
"значение или превышает допустимые значения."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1278
msgid ""
"Raised when an attempt is made to insert an :class:`Attr` node that is "
"already present elsewhere in the document."
msgstr ""
"Возникает при попытке вставить узел :class:`Attr`, который уже присутствует "
"где-либо в документе."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1284
msgid ""
"Raised if a parameter or an operation is not supported on the underlying "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Возникает, если параметр или операция не поддерживается базовым объектом."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1289
msgid ""
"This exception is raised when a string parameter contains a character that "
"is not permitted in the context it's being used in by the XML 1.0 "
"recommendation. For example, attempting to create an :class:`Element` node "
"with a space in the element type name will cause this error to be raised."
msgstr ""
"Это исключение возникает, когда строковый параметр содержит символ, который "
"не разрешен в контексте, в котором он используется согласно рекомендации XML "
"1.0. Например, попытка создать узел :class:`Element` с пробелом в имени типа "
"элемента приведет к возникновению этой ошибки."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1297
msgid "Raised when an attempt is made to modify the type of a node."
msgstr "Возникает при попытке изменить тип узла."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1302
msgid ""
"Raised when an attempt is made to use an object that is not defined or is no "
"longer usable."
msgstr ""
"Возникает, когда предпринимается попытка использовать объект, который не "
"определен или больше не пригоден для использования."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1308
msgid ""
"If an attempt is made to change any object in a way that is not permitted "
"with regard to the `Namespaces in XML <https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml-names/"
">`_ recommendation, this exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"Если предпринята попытка изменить какой-либо объект способом, который не "
"разрешен в соответствии с рекомендацией `Пространства имен в XML <https://"
"www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml-names/>`_, это исключение поднят."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1315
msgid ""
"Exception when a node does not exist in the referenced context.  For "
"example, :meth:`NamedNodeMap.removeNamedItem` will raise this if the node "
"passed in does not exist in the map."
msgstr ""
"Исключение, когда узел не существует в указанном контексте. Например, :meth:"
"`NamedNodeMap.removeNamedItem` вызовет это, если переданный узел не "
"существует на карте."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1322
msgid ""
"Raised when the implementation does not support the requested type of object "
"or operation."
msgstr ""
"Возникает, когда реализация не поддерживает запрошенный тип объекта или "
"операции."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1328
msgid ""
"This is raised if data is specified for a node which does not support data."
msgstr ""
"Это возникает, если данные указаны для узла, который не поддерживает данные."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1335
msgid ""
"Raised on attempts to modify an object where modifications are not allowed "
"(such as for read-only nodes)."
msgstr ""
"Возникает при попытках изменить объект, в котором изменения не разрешены "
"(например, для узлов, доступных только для чтения)."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1341
msgid "Raised when an invalid or illegal string is specified."
msgstr "Возникает, когда указана недопустимая или недопустимая строка."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1348
msgid ""
"Raised when an operation would make the document invalid with respect to "
"partial validity. This is not known to be used in the Python DOM "
"implementations, but may be received from DOM implementations not written in "
"Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1356
msgid ""
"Raised when a node is inserted in a different document than it currently "
"belongs to, and the implementation does not support migrating the node from "
"one document to the other."
msgstr ""
"Возникает, когда узел вставлен в документ, отличный от того, которому он "
"принадлежит в данный момент, и реализация не поддерживает миграцию узла из "
"одного документа в другой."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1361
msgid ""
"The exception codes defined in the DOM recommendation map to the exceptions "
"described above according to this table:"
msgstr ""
"Коды исключений, определенные в рекомендациях DOM, соответствуют "
"исключениям, описанным выше, в соответствии с этой таблицей:"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1365
msgid "Constant"
msgstr "Константа"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1365
msgid "Exception"
msgstr "Исключение"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1367
msgid ":exc:`DomstringSizeErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`DomstringSizeErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1369
msgid ":exc:`HierarchyRequestErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`HierarchyRequestErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1371
msgid ":exc:`IndexSizeErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`IndexSizeErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1373
msgid ":exc:`InuseAttributeErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`InuseAttributeErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1375
msgid ":exc:`InvalidAccessErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`InvalidAccessErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1377
msgid ":exc:`InvalidCharacterErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`InvalidCharacterErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1379
msgid ":exc:`InvalidModificationErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`InvalidModificationErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1381
msgid ":exc:`InvalidStateErr`"
msgstr ":exc:`InvalidStateErr`"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1383
